<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;KHENTKAUS I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Khentkaus I, also known as Khentkawes, was a queen of ancient Egypt during the 4th dynasty and may have been a daughter of Menkaure, wife of Shepseskaf and Userkaf, and mother of Sahure."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENKAURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menkaure was a pharaoh of the 4th dynasty and father to Khentkaus I, whose pyramid complex is close to his."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHEPSESKAF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shepseskaf was a king of the 4th dynasty and husband to Khentkaus I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USERKAF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Userkaf was a king of the 4th dynasty and husband to Khentkaus I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAHURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sahure was a son of Khentkaus I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASTABA AT GIZA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mastaba at Giza, tomb LG100, is the burial site of Khentkaus I and is located near Menkaure's pyramid complex."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENKAURE'S PYRAMID COMPLEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menkaure's pyramid complex is the area around Menkaure's pyramid, which is close to Khentkaus I's Mastaba at Giza."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRAMID CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyramid city is a settlement near the pyramid complex, constructed from unbaked mud-brick and covered in yellow plaster, likely housing priests and servants."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIZA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Giza is the location where Khentkaus I's Mastaba and Menkaure's pyramid complex are situated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURTH DYNASTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 4th dynasty refers to the period in ancient Egyptian history during which Khentkaus I lived and ruled."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARAOH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharaoh is the title given to the rulers of ancient Egypt, such as Menkaure and Khentkaus I's father."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Queen is the title given to female rulers or wives of pharaohs, such as Khentkaus I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"King is the title given to male rulers or husbands of queens, such as Shepseskaf and Userkaf."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Son is the title given to male offspring, such as Sahure, who is a son of Khentkaus I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAUGHTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Daughter is the title given to female offspring, such as Khentkaus I, who may be a daughter of Menkaure."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Priest is a religious official who served in the pyramid city, likely part of the pyramid complex's personnel."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERVANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Servant is a general term for individuals who worked in the pyramid city, likely part of the pyramid complex's personnel."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGAZINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magazine is a storage area within the houses of the pyramid city, used to store goods."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRANARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Granary is a storage area within the houses of the pyramid city, used to store grain."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNBAKED MUD-BRICK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unbaked mud-brick is the construction material used for the pyramid city."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW PLASTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow plaster is the surface covering used for the pyramid city."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;KHENTKAUS I&quot;" target="&quot;MENKAURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">12.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Khentkaus I may be a daughter of Menkaure based on the close proximity of their pyramid complexes."</data>
      <data key="d5">"family relationship, proximity"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KHENTKAUS I&quot;" target="&quot;SHEPSESKAF&quot;">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Khentkaus I was married to Shepseskaf, indicating a marital relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, spouse"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KHENTKAUS I&quot;" target="&quot;USERKAF&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Khentkaus I was married to Userkaf, indicating a marital relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, spouse"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KHENTKAUS I&quot;" target="&quot;SAHURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sahure is a son of Khentkaus I, indicating a parent-child relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"parent-child, lineage"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MASTABA AT GIZA&quot;" target="&quot;MENKAURE'S PYRAMID COMPLEX&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mastaba at Giza is located very close to Menkaure's pyramid complex, suggesting a possible family relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proximity, family relationship"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MENKAURE'S PYRAMID COMPLEX&quot;" target="&quot;PYRAMID CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The pyramid city is located near Menkaure's pyramid complex, likely serving the needs of the pyramid complex's personnel."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proximity, service area"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
